sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: Proposed durable handoff and delivery retry sequence
    accDescr: Processing commits an enriched event and outbox intent before acknowledging the original event. A relay publishes durable delivery work. Failed delivery schedules a bounded retry without calling enrichment again. A successful endpoint response is persisted before completion. Crashes can still cause duplicates, a stable event identifier supports deduplication.
    participant B as Event buffer
    participant P as Processing
    participant S as Event state + outbox
    participant R as Outbox relay
    participant Q as Delivery work
    participant D as Delivery
    participant E as Customer endpoint
    B->>P: Receive event
    Note over P: Obtain enrichment result before committing
    P->>S: Commit result + delivery intent atomically
    S-->>P: Durable commit confirmed
    P->>B: Acknowledge event
    R->>S: Read pending intent
    R->>Q: Publish delivery work
    Q-->>R: Durable publish confirmed
    R->>S: Mark intent dispatched
    Note over S,Q: Relay may publish twice after a crash, use stable delivery ID
    Q->>D: Claim due work with lease
    D->>E: POST enriched payload + stable event ID
    E-->>D: Retryable failure
    D->>Q: Durably reschedule with backoff + jitter
    Note over Q,E: Bounded attempts / age, permanent failures go to recovery
    Q->>D: Claim retry when due
    D->>E: POST same payload + event ID
    E-->>D: Success response
    D->>S: Persist successful outcome
    S-->>D: Durable commit confirmed
    D->>Q: Complete work
    Note over D,E: Response loss or crash can repeat delivery, recipient deduplicates
